  note         = {Preprint. The absorption order on $78$ union groups is a
                  partial order (A1) characterizing datum-equality when
                  $C_G\ne\emptyset$ (A2), with
                  dominance pruning (A3); the redundancy rank $\rho$ satisfies
                  disjoint superadditivity (R3$'$), the general corollary
                  (R3$''$), the overlap-deficit bound (T), and the
                  absorption-collapse formula and minimum-core uniqueness
                  for distinct $G\preceq H$ with $C_H\ne\emptyset$ (R4$'$).
                  Singleton factorization uses a finite ambient family
                  containing $S$, with no singleton on $S_0$ in that family.
                  The cited census reports $7{,}052{,}450$ minimal
                  $u$-covers of $\mathbb{Z}/35$; this count is not Lean-certified.
                  The ES forcing spectrum contributes the
                  repaired forced-cell characterization S2(a)$'$, S2(b--d),
                  partition S3, and union-max S4. For the two-sided forcing
                  decomposition, A checks only that each $H\in\mathrm{HardClasses}$
                  maps to OpenKClasses under $((H-1)/24)\bmod35$ (natural-number
                  division), plus the separate
                  equivalence $(k\bmod7\in\{0,1,5\}\land
                  k\bmod5\in\{0,2\})\Leftrightarrow k\in\mathrm{OpenKClasses}$
                  for natural $k<35$; B and C are the named scaling
                  and filter lemmas under their stated hypotheses.
                  D checks that $35/\gcd(m',35)$ is in
                  $\{1,5,7,35\}$ for natural $m'>0$, and that for natural $r<7$ the set
                  $\{r,r+7,r+14,r+21,r+28\}$ is not contained in OpenKClasses.
                  Writing $m'=f.\mathrm{mprime}$, its singleton lemma proves only
                  $|\mathrm{covered}(f)|=1\Rightarrow35\mid m'$ given
                  $|\mathrm{covered}(f)|=35/\gcd(m',35)$ and $m'>0$
                  (the additional $hC$ premise is tautological).
                  The general congruence export, the covered-set/progression
                  bridge, the cardinality-formula derivation, and the surgical prime-covering/hard-cell
                  biconditional assembly remain UNFORMALIZED.
                  These declarations, together with the listed absorption and
                  forcing-spectrum results, were checked
                  in Lean 4.34.1 + Mathlib v4.34.1 (modules
                  Mathproofs/ESAbsorptionOrder.lean,
                  Mathproofs/ESForcingSpectrum.lean,
                  Mathproofs/ESForcingDecomp.lean; bakkie \texttt{lake build}
                  exit 0, zero sorrys, standard axioms only, as historically recorded).
                  The October 11 PDF is superseded; consult the corrected source.
                  The surgical
                  down-set A4 is left [OPEN].},
